		{
			dependencies: ["5630715FB28AA469"]
			description: [
				"Use a backpack for the road, drawers for large quantities of repeated materials, and Tom's Storage for searchable access across many containers. Each tool solves a different storage problem."
				"Do not build the final warehouse on day one. Start with labelled zones, watch what actually accumulates, and expand the system around real needs."
				"Keep irreplaceable maps, relics and breeding items in clearly named storage instead of feeding everything into automatic bulk systems."
				"Storage should have layers: backpack for the road, drawers for bulk, ordinary labelled containers for unique objects, and a searchable terminal across the room. One giant unsorted network only hides disorder behind a search bar."
